{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgf7CZoD9dGdn1KBfT2xR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Gz2ReCHLSqDBzkJJoLNX95","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/ref && for f in README.md index.html package.json; do gh api repos/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/contents/dist/handoff/$f -H \"Accept: application/vnd.github.raw\" > eng_$f; done; cat eng_README.md eng_index.html eng_package.json; gh api repos/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/contents/dist/handoff/game --jq '.[].name'; gh api repos/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/contents/dist/handoff/kits --jq '.[].name'; gh api repos/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/contents/dist/handoff/modules --jq '.[].name'"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":599,"cache_read_input_tokens":23422,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":599,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"45e6dbf6-73de-492d-a24c-c1459c8eed93","uuid":"28f9aa7b-2791-4d00-9fb5-61a88b85c586","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:13:48.907Z","request_id":"req_011Cgf7CZR9AQTCqT7r4RPJL","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Gz2ReCHLSqDBzkJJoLNX95":{"command":"cd /tmp/ref && for f in README.md index.html package.json; do gh api repos/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/contents/dist/handoff/$f -H \"Accept: application/vnd.github.raw\" > eng_$f; done; cat eng_README.md eng_index.html eng_package.json; gh api repos/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/contents/dist/handoff/game --jq '.[].name'; gh api repos/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/contents/dist/handoff/kits --jq '.[].name'; gh api repos/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/contents/dist/handoff/modules --jq '.[].name'"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Gz2ReCHLSqDBzkJJoLNX95","type":"tool_result","content":"# my-3D2dge handoff package (v0.85.1)\n\nEverything a coding agent needs to build, run, test and check a game on the full my-3D2dge engine, in one folder of text\nfiles. You don't need the engine's repository, and you don't need to read the engine's source below its header.\n\n## Start here\n\n1. **Read `API.md`**, the API card: a complete game to start from, what x, y and z mean in each view, the rules, the\n   common mistakes and the API by area. It is the one page to read whole.\n2. **Start from a game, not an empty file.** The kit for your genre (`kits/`): the card's Genre playbook names one for\n   each genre, and `kits/README.md` says which file is which. `kits/<id>.js` is a complete game in that genre, readable\n   (its title, play and end, the modules it rests on, sound, touch controls), `kits/<id>.html` plays it, and\n   `node kits/test.mjs <id>` runs it headless. Or the template, `game/`: a small complete game (climbing, a guard with\n   sight, an HTML HUD, scenes) that `game/index.html` plays and `game/test.mjs` tests without a browser. Copy one into\n   `game/` and make it yours.\n3. **Search `API-INDEX.md`** when you need a name: every public name in the engine, one line each, with its signature,\n   units and defaults, and the height rules at the top. `grep -n \"ledge\\|landing\" API-INDEX.md`. Don't read it whole.\n4. **`AI_GUIDE.md`** has the recipes: genre by genre, the look to aim for, the frame order, heights, recorded sessions.\n5. **Don't build a pause menu, settings, key rebinding, full screen or a loading screen**: every game has them (`API.md`,\n   \"Standard features\"). Adjust them with `new E.Game({ menu: { items, settings, controls, quit } })`; heavy setup goes in\n   `game.start({ boot: { steps } })`.\n6. **Objects without drawing code:** read `docs/ASSETS.md` whole before you draw a barrel, a table or a tree.\n   `r.shape('barrel', x, y, 0, { facing })` draws one of the core library's in every view; `node tools/asset-find.mjs\n   \"market stall\"` searches it and the store (`src/assets/sets/`: about a thousand objects, materials and sprites,\n   each with where it came from), and `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs mine.js#stool` draws one you wrote, to look at\n   before you use it.\n\n## What is here\n\n| File | What it is |\n| --- | --- |\n| `my-3d2dge.js` | the full engine, readable (one file, no dependencies): the core, then every module |\n| `modules/` | each engine module on its own, when there are any (one general system; its header is its manual), to load after the agent edition |\n| `my-3d2dge-agent.js` | the agent edition: the essential engine, whose header is a shorter manual (a game written for it runs on the full engine) |\n| `API.md`, `API-INDEX.md`, `AI_GUIDE.md` | the card, the index, the guide |\n| `kits/` | the 2D genre kits, readable: each kit's game (`<id>.js`) and the page that plays it (`<id>.html`), the table of them (`README.md`) and their headless test (`test.mjs`) |\n| `game/` | the template game: `index.html`, `game.js`, `test.mjs` |\n| `tools/check.mjs` | plays a game in headless Chromium, switches its views, and reports errors, what is on screen, and `game.debug.snapshot()` |\n| `tools/filmstrip.mjs` | records frames into one picture, to judge motion (`--seed 1` makes it repeatable, `--compare` marks what changed) |\n| `tools/replay.mjs` | replays a recorded play session exactly (`E.session`, a bug seen on a phone) |\n| `docs/ASSETS.md` | the asset card: still objects and materials as data (`r.shape`, `map.solid`, `E.MATERIALS`), the core library, writing one |\n| `tools/asset-find.mjs`, `asset-sheet.mjs`, `asset-set.mjs` | search the core library and the store; draw an object in every view and lint it; cut the few entries a game uses into a set of its own (`asset-lib.mjs` is theirs) |\n| `src/assets/` | the asset store: sets of objects and materials converted from CC0 libraries (Kenney, KayKit, ambientCG), with their catalogs. A game loads one with its script and `E.addAssets(window.ASSETS['kenney-furniture'])`; the Asset Lab shows them all at my-3d2dge.vercel.app/asset-lab |\n| `package.json` | pins Playwright for the tools |\n\nNot here: the 3D engine (three.js and Rapier) and its kits, the playbook's 3D rows. They are on the site\n(my-3d2dge.vercel.app/3d) and in the repository (github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge); here a 3D game is built on the 2D\nengine's views (`kits/README.md`, 3D).\n\n## Run, test, check\n\n```sh\nnpm install                          # Playwright, for the tools (once)\nnpx playwright install chromium      # its browser (once)\nnode game/test.mjs                   # the game's headless test: no browser, a second\nnode tools/check.mjs game/index.html # play it in a browser: errors, screenshots, its snapshot\nnode kits/test.mjs arcade            # a kit, headless: it plays, and its proof gives the same hash twice\nnode tools/check.mjs kits/arcade.html#arcade/maze   # a kit in a browser, at a part (its deep link)\nnode tools/filmstrip.mjs game/index.html --steps \"wait:800 press:Enter wait:500 rec:16:2 down:KeyD wait:600\" --seed 1\n```\n\nOpen `game/index.html` in a browser to play (or serve the folder: `npx serve`). To hand a single file to a person, inline\nthe two scripts into the page.\n\n## Testing a game without a browser\n\n`new E.Game()` is headless in Node (or with `{ headless: true }`): no screen, sound or DOM, and `draw` is skipped.\n\n- `game.advance(seconds)` runs exact fixed steps of 1/120 s at once: `advance(1)` is 120 updates.\n- `game.input.tap('jump')` presses an action for one step, `hold('right')` holds one down, `hold('right', false)` lets go.\n- `game.debug = { snapshot() { return {...} }, teleport(x, y, z) {...} }` is your game's handle: tests read it, and\n  `tools/check.mjs` and `tools/replay.mjs` print it.\n- `game.stop()`, `game.start()` and `game.dispose()` stop, resume and end a game.\n\nThe same inputs give the same game on every machine and at every refresh rate: the clock is an exact fixed step.\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>my-3D2dge handoff package</title>\n<style>\n  :root { color-scheme: light dark; --ink: #1b1726; --paper: #f6f3ee; --line: #d8d2c8; --accent: #6a4ad0 }\n  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { :root { --ink: #ece8f6; --paper: #15121c; --line: #3a3348; --accent: #a68cff } }\n  body { margin: 0; background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink); font: 16px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif }\n  main { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px 16px 48px }\n  h1 { font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 0 0 .25rem } p { margin: .5rem 0 1rem }\n  ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line) }\n  li { padding: .6rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line) } a { color: var(--accent); font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace }\n  li span { display: block; font-size: .9rem; opacity: .8 }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<main>\n<h1>my-3D2dge handoff package</h1>\n<p>v0.85.1 · dev-build. Everything a coding agent needs to build, run, test and check a game on the full engine, as text files. Start with <a href=\"README.md\">README.md</a>, then read <a href=\"API.md\">API.md</a>. Play <a href=\"kits/README.md\">a genre kit</a> or <a href=\"game/index.html\">the template game</a>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"README.md\">README.md</a><span>start here: what the package holds, which page to read, how to run and test a game</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"package.json\">package.json</a><span>pins Playwright for the tools</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"my-3d2dge.js\">my-3d2dge.js</a><span>the full engine, readable: the core and every module</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"my-3d2dge-agent.js\">my-3d2dge-agent.js</a><span>the agent edition: the essential engine, its header a short manual</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/arcade.js\">modules/arcade.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/click.js\">modules/click.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: point-and-click adventures: walk areas with holes, depth, hotspots, verbs, an inventory</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/drive.js\">modules/drive.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: cars on the ground plane, a race round a track, the drivers who race it</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/fight.js\">modules/fight.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: one-on-one fighting: fighters with frame data, guards, throws, specials, a meter; rounds; a CPU; training</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/gen.js\">modules/gen.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: generated maps: rooms and corridors, BSP, caves, mazes and scatter, from a seed</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/grid.js\">modules/grid.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: square and hex grids: paths, ranges, lines, fields of view, fog, groups, movers and turns</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/mode7.js\">modules/mode7.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: a perspective floor drawn a row at a time, a sky that turns with it, everything on it scaled by its distance</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/physics.js\">modules/physics.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: 2D rigid bodies: circles, boxes, polygons, segments; fast balls that never pass through</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/rhythm.js\">modules/rhythm.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: charts on a song's steps, judged on the music clock: combos, grades, holds, a highway</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/road.js\">modules/road.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/rooms.js\">modules/rooms.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: a world of rooms joined at their edges, the map of what was explored, gates and saves</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/rpg.js\">modules/rpg.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: items, inventories, equipment, shops, a party's stats and levels, status, damage, encounters</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/songs.js\">modules/songs.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: the songbook: the kits' best songs and more, and jingles, tagged by mood</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/story.js\">modules/story.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: dialogue as data, flags and values, a quest log and emote balloons</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/strategy.js\">modules/strategy.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: real-time strategy and simulation: selection, orders, armies, production, resources, placement, fog, AI; a day clock, needs, overlays</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/terrain.js\">modules/terrain.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: destructible ground in the side plane: carved and added, walked on, drawn in chunks</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"API.md\">API.md</a><span>the API card: read it whole</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"API-INDEX.md\">API-INDEX.md</a><span>every public name, one line each: search it</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"AI_GUIDE.md\">AI_GUIDE.md</a><span>the guide: recipes, the look, heights, sessions</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"tools/check.mjs\">tools/check.mjs</a><span>plays a game headless and reports errors, screenshots and its snapshot</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"tools/filmstrip.mjs\">tools/filmstrip.mjs</a><span>records frames into one picture</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"tools/replay.mjs\">tools/replay.mjs</a><span>replays a recorded play session exactly</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"docs/ASSETS.md\">docs/ASSETS.md</a><span>the asset card: objects and materials as data (r.shape), the core library, writing one</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"tools/asset-find.mjs\">tools/asset-find.mjs</a><span>searches the core library and the store: node tools/asset-find.mjs \"tavern table\"</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"tools/asset-sheet.mjs\">tools/asset-sheet.mjs</a><span>draws an object in every view and says what reads badly</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"tools/asset-set.mjs\">tools/asset-set.mjs</a><span>cuts the few entries a game uses from the store's sets</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"tools/asset-lib.mjs\">tools/asset-lib.mjs</a><span>shared by the asset tools</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"game/game.js\">game/game.js</a><span>the template game: copy it</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"game/index.html\">game/index.html</a><span>the template game: play it</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"game/test.mjs\">game/test.mjs</a><span>its headless test: node game/test.mjs</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"kits/README.md\">kits/</a><span>the 22 genre kits, readable: each kit's game and the page that plays it (kits/arcade.html), the table of them, and their headless test (node kits/test.mjs)</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"src/assets/README.md\">src/assets/</a><span>the asset store: 29 sets of objects and materials converted from CC0 libraries, and their catalogs (docs/ASSETS.md, \"Make one\")</span></li>\n</ul>\n</main>\n</body>\n</html>\n{\n  \"name\": \"my-3d2dge-handoff\",\n  \"version\": \"0.85.1\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"description\": \"my-3D2dge for coding agents: the engine, its card, index and guide, the tools and a template game\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"test\": \"node game/test.mjs\",\n    \"check\": \"node tools/check.mjs game/index.html\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"playwright\": \"1.63.0\"\n  }\n}\ngame.js\nindex.html\ntest.mjs\nREADME.md\nadventure.html\nadventure.js\nanimlab.html\nanimlab.js\narcade.html\narcade.js\nartillery.html\nartillery.js\nbrawler.html\nbrawler.js\nfighting.html\nfighting.js\nkart.html\nkart.js\nmetroidvania.html\nmetroidvania.js\npinball.html\npinball.js\nplatformer.html\nplatformer.js\npointclick.html\npointclick.js\npuzzle.html\npuzzle.js\nrhythm.html\nrhythm.js\nroad.html\nroad.js\nroguelike.html\nroguelike.js\nrpg.html\nrpg.js\nrts.html\nrts.js\nshooter.html\nshooter.js\nsim.html\nsim.js\nsports.html\nsports.js\nstealth.html\nstealth.js\ntactics.html\ntactics.js\ntest.mjs\narcade.js\nclick.js\ndrive.js\nfight.js\ngen.js\ngrid.js\nmode7.js\nphysics.js\nrhythm.js\nroad.js\nrooms.js\nrpg.js\nsongs.js\nstory.js\nstrategy.js\nterrain.js\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-181337__x3ec78e/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"45e6dbf6-73de-492d-a24c-c1459c8eed93","uuid":"722ce60f-46c0-4916-9279-c7d3fb4f76bb","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:13:51.271Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# my-3D2dge handoff package (v0.85.1)\n\nEverything a coding agent needs to build, run, test and check a game on the full my-3D2dge engine, in one folder of text\nfiles. You don't need the engine's repository, and you don't need to read the engine's source below its header.\n\n## Start here\n\n1. **Read `API.md`**, the API card: a complete game to start from, what x, y and z mean in each view, the rules, the\n   common mistakes and the API by area. It is the one page to read whole.\n2. **Start from a game, not an empty file.** The kit for your genre (`kits/`): the card's Genre playbook names one for\n   each genre, and `kits/README.md` says which file is which. `kits/<id>.js` is a complete game in that genre, readable\n   (its title, play and end, the modules it rests on, sound, touch controls), `kits/<id>.html` plays it, and\n   `node kits/test.mjs <id>` runs it headless. Or the template, `game/`: a small complete game (climbing, a guard with\n   sight, an HTML HUD, scenes) that `game/index.html` plays and `game/test.mjs` tests without a browser. Copy one into\n   `game/` and make it yours.\n3. **Search `API-INDEX.md`** when you need a name: every public name in the engine, one line each, with its signature,\n   units and defaults, and the height rules at the top. `grep -n \"ledge\\|landing\" API-INDEX.md`. Don't read it whole.\n4. **`AI_GUIDE.md`** has the recipes: genre by genre, the look to aim for, the frame order, heights, recorded sessions.\n5. **Don't build a pause menu, settings, key rebinding, full screen or a loading screen**: every game has them (`API.md`,\n   \"Standard features\"). Adjust them with `new E.Game({ menu: { items, settings, controls, quit } })`; heavy setup goes in\n   `game.start({ boot: { steps } })`.\n6. **Objects without drawing code:** read `docs/ASSETS.md` whole before you draw a barrel, a table or a tree.\n   `r.shape('barrel', x, y, 0, { facing })` draws one of the core library's in every view; `node tools/asset-find.mjs\n   \"market stall\"` searches it and the store (`src/assets/sets/`: about a thousand objects, materials and sprites,\n   each with where it came from), and `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs mine.js#stool` draws one you wrote, to look at\n   before you use it.\n\n## What is here\n\n| File | What it is |\n| --- | --- |\n| `my-3d2dge.js` | the full engine, readable (one file, no dependencies): the core, then every module |\n| `modules/` | each engine module on its own, when there are any (one general system; its header is its manual), to load after the agent edition |\n| `my-3d2dge-agent.js` | the agent edition: the essential engine, whose header is a shorter manual (a game written for it runs on the full engine) |\n| `API.md`, `API-INDEX.md`, `AI_GUIDE.md` | the card, the index, the guide |\n| `kits/` | the 2D genre kits, readable: each kit's game (`<id>.js`) and the page that plays it (`<id>.html`), the table of them (`README.md`) and their headless test (`test.mjs`) |\n| `game/` | the template game: `index.html`, `game.js`, `test.mjs` |\n| `tools/check.mjs` | plays a game in headless Chromium, switches its views, and reports errors, what is on screen, and `game.debug.snapshot()` |\n| `tools/filmstrip.mjs` | records frames into one picture, to judge motion (`--seed 1` makes it repeatable, `--compare` marks what changed) |\n| `tools/replay.mjs` | replays a recorded play session exactly (`E.session`, a bug seen on a phone) |\n| `docs/ASSETS.md` | the asset card: still objects and materials as data (`r.shape`, `map.solid`, `E.MATERIALS`), the core library, writing one |\n| `tools/asset-find.mjs`, `asset-sheet.mjs`, `asset-set.mjs` | search the core library and the store; draw an object in every view and lint it; cut the few entries a game uses into a set of its own (`asset-lib.mjs` is theirs) |\n| `src/assets/` | the asset store: sets of objects and materials converted from CC0 libraries (Kenney, KayKit, ambientCG), with their catalogs. A game loads one with its script and `E.addAssets(window.ASSETS['kenney-furniture'])`; the Asset Lab shows them all at my-3d2dge.vercel.app/asset-lab |\n| `package.json` | pins Playwright for the tools |\n\nNot here: the 3D engine (three.js and Rapier) and its kits, the playbook's 3D rows. They are on the site\n(my-3d2dge.vercel.app/3d) and in the repository (github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge); here a 3D game is built on the 2D\nengine's views (`kits/README.md`, 3D).\n\n## Run, test, check\n\n```sh\nnpm install                          # Playwright, for the tools (once)\nnpx playwright install chromium      # its browser (once)\nnode game/test.mjs                   # the game's headless test: no browser, a second\nnode tools/check.mjs game/index.html # play it in a browser: errors, screenshots, its snapshot\nnode kits/test.mjs arcade            # a kit, headless: it plays, and its proof gives the same hash twice\nnode tools/check.mjs kits/arcade.html#arcade/maze   # a kit in a browser, at a part (its deep link)\nnode tools/filmstrip.mjs game/index.html --steps \"wait:800 press:Enter wait:500 rec:16:2 down:KeyD wait:600\" --seed 1\n```\n\nOpen `game/index.html` in a browser to play (or serve the folder: `npx serve`). To hand a single file to a person, inline\nthe two scripts into the page.\n\n## Testing a game without a browser\n\n`new E.Game()` is headless in Node (or with `{ headless: true }`): no screen, sound or DOM, and `draw` is skipped.\n\n- `game.advance(seconds)` runs exact fixed steps of 1/120 s at once: `advance(1)` is 120 updates.\n- `game.input.tap('jump')` presses an action for one step, `hold('right')` holds one down, `hold('right', false)` lets go.\n- `game.debug = { snapshot() { return {...} }, teleport(x, y, z) {...} }` is your game's handle: tests read it, and\n  `tools/check.mjs` and `tools/replay.mjs` print it.\n- `game.stop()`, `game.start()` and `game.dispose()` stop, resume and end a game.\n\nThe same inputs give the same game on every machine and at every refresh rate: the clock is an exact fixed step.\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>my-3D2dge handoff package</title>\n<style>\n  :root { color-scheme: light dark; --ink: #1b1726; --paper: #f6f3ee; --line: #d8d2c8; --accent: #6a4ad0 }\n  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { :root { --ink: #ece8f6; --paper: #15121c; --line: #3a3348; --accent: #a68cff } }\n  body { margin: 0; background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink); font: 16px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif }\n  main { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px 16px 48px }\n  h1 { font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 0 0 .25rem } p { margin: .5rem 0 1rem }\n  ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line) }\n  li { padding: .6rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line) } a { color: var(--accent); font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace }\n  li span { display: block; font-size: .9rem; opacity: .8 }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<main>\n<h1>my-3D2dge handoff package</h1>\n<p>v0.85.1 · dev-build. Everything a coding agent needs to build, run, test and check a game on the full engine, as text files. Start with <a href=\"README.md\">README.md</a>, then read <a href=\"API.md\">API.md</a>. Play <a href=\"kits/README.md\">a genre kit</a> or <a href=\"game/index.html\">the template game</a>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"README.md\">README.md</a><span>start here: what the package holds, which page to read, how to run and test a game</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"package.json\">package.json</a><span>pins Playwright for the tools</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"my-3d2dge.js\">my-3d2dge.js</a><span>the full engine, readable: the core and every module</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"my-3d2dge-agent.js\">my-3d2dge-agent.js</a><span>the agent edition: the essential engine, its header a short manual</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/arcade.js\">modules/arcade.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/click.js\">modules/click.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: point-and-click adventures: walk areas with holes, depth, hotspots, verbs, an inventory</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/drive.js\">modules/drive.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: cars on the ground plane, a race round a track, the drivers who race it</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/fight.js\">modules/fight.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: one-on-one fighting: fighters with frame data, guards, throws, specials, a meter; rounds; a CPU; training</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/gen.js\">modules/gen.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: generated maps: rooms and corridors, BSP, caves, mazes and scatter, from a seed</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/grid.js\">modules/grid.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: square and hex grids: paths, ranges, lines, fields of view, fog, groups, movers and turns</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/mode7.js\">modules/mode7.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: a perspective floor drawn a row at a time, a sky that turns with it, everything on it scaled by its distance</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/physics.js\">modules/physics.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: 2D rigid bodies: circles, boxes, polygons, segments; fast balls that never pass through</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/rhythm.js\">modules/rhythm.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: charts on a song's steps, judged on the music clock: combos, grades, holds, a highway</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/road.js\">modules/road.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/rooms.js\">modules/rooms.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: a world of rooms joined at their edges, the map of what was explored, gates and saves</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/rpg.js\">modules/rpg.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: items, inventories, equipment, shops, a party's stats and levels, status, damage, encounters</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/songs.js\">modules/songs.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: the songbook: the kits' best songs and more, and jingles, tagged by mood</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/story.js\">modules/story.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: dialogue as data, flags and values, a quest log and emote balloons</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/strategy.js\">modules/strategy.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: real-time strategy and simulation: selection, orders, armies, production, resources, placement, fog, AI; a day clock, needs, overlays</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"modules/terrain.js\">modules/terrain.js</a><span>a module, loaded after the engine: destructible ground in the side plane: carved and added, walked on, drawn in chunks</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"API.md\">API.md</a><span>the API card: read it whole</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"API-INDEX.md\">API-INDEX.md</a><span>every public name, one line each: search it</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"AI_GUIDE.md\">AI_GUIDE.md</a><span>the guide: recipes, the look, heights, sessions</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"tools/check.mjs\">tools/check.mjs</a><span>plays a game headless and reports errors, screenshots and its snapshot</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"tools/filmstrip.mjs\">tools/filmstrip.mjs</a><span>records frames into one picture</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"tools/replay.mjs\">tools/replay.mjs</a><span>replays a recorded play session exactly</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"docs/ASSETS.md\">docs/ASSETS.md</a><span>the asset card: objects and materials as data (r.shape), the core library, writing one</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"tools/asset-find.mjs\">tools/asset-find.mjs</a><span>searches the core library and the store: node tools/asset-find.mjs \"tavern table\"</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"tools/asset-sheet.mjs\">tools/asset-sheet.mjs</a><span>draws an object in every view and says what reads badly</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"tools/asset-set.mjs\">tools/asset-set.mjs</a><span>cuts the few entries a game uses from the store's sets</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"tools/asset-lib.mjs\">tools/asset-lib.mjs</a><span>shared by the asset tools</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"game/game.js\">game/game.js</a><span>the template game: copy it</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"game/index.html\">game/index.html</a><span>the template game: play it</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"game/test.mjs\">game/test.mjs</a><span>its headless test: node game/test.mjs</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"kits/README.md\">kits/</a><span>the 22 genre kits, readable: each kit's game and the page that plays it (kits/arcade.html), the table of them, and their headless test (node kits/test.mjs)</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"src/assets/README.md\">src/assets/</a><span>the asset store: 29 sets of objects and materials converted from CC0 libraries, and their catalogs (docs/ASSETS.md, \"Make one\")</span></li>\n</ul>\n</main>\n</body>\n</html>\n{\n  \"name\": \"my-3d2dge-handoff\",\n  \